.TH PATH_FNMATCH 3
.SH NAME
path_fnmatch \- shell-style filename pattern matching
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "path_internal.h"
.PP
.B int path_fnmatch(const char* pattern, unsigned int plen, const char* string, unsigned int slen, int flags);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_fnmatch
checks if the 
.I string 
(of length 
.I slen
) matches the specified 
.I pattern 
(of length 
.I plen
).
.PP
It supports standard shell wildcards like '*' and '?', as well as character classes '[...]'. The 
.I flags
parameter controls behavior such as path separators and period handling (e.g., PATH_FNM_PATHNAME).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 if the string matches the pattern, or 
.B PATH_FNM_NOMATCH
if it does not.